WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:15.437
Unit twenty-one: Gender Equality. Today you will say what is right with 'should' + passive.

4
00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:18.378
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:22.543
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:24.698
Equality.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:28.530
Equality means having the same rights and chances.

8
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.337
Equality makes society stronger.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.707
Your turn. Say: Equality.

10
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.637
Equality.

11
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.582
Opportunity.

12
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:44.198
Opportunity means a chance to do something.

13
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:47.642
Every girl deserves the opportunity to study.

14
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.030
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

15
00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:54.972
Opportunity.

16
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:56.671
Rights.

17
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.426
Rights means what every person is allowed to have.

18
00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:03.097
Education is one of our rights.

19
00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:05.894
Your turn. Say: Rights.

20
00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:09.862
Rights.

21
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:11.873
Stereotype.

22
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:16.648
Stereotype means a fixed, unfair idea about a group.

23
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.609
'Boys don't cook' is a stereotype.

24
00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:22.823
Your turn. Say: Stereotype.

25
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.912
Stereotype.

26
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.790
Education.

27
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:32.456
Education means learning at school and beyond.

28
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.154
Education changes lives.

29
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.275
Your turn. Say: Education.

30
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.285
Education.

31
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.086
Leadership.

32
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:47.118
Leadership means guiding a group.

33
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:50.285
She showed great leadership as class president.

34
00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:53.605
Your turn. Say: Leadership.

35
00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.410
Leadership.

36
00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:58.663
Fair.

37
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.568
Fair means treating people equally.

38
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:04.508
The rules should be fair to everyone.

39
00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:07.270
Your turn. Say: Fair.

40
00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:10.949
Fair.

41
00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.673
Respect.

42
00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:15.822
Respect means treating people well.

43
00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:17.987
Respect starts at home.

44
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:21.050
Your turn. Say: Respect.

45
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:24.762
Respect.

46
00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:29.728
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.488
Visal, what can schools do to promote equality?

48
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.964
Everyone should be treated fairly, boys and girls.

49
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.260
How can that happen?

50
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:45.625
Girls should be encouraged to lead, and boys should be taught to cook.

51
00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.414
And stereotypes?

52
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:55.710
Stereotypes should be challenged in class. Everyone deserves the same opportunity.

53
00:02:56.867 --> 00:02:58.239
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:01.849
Grammar focus: Should plus passive.

55
00:03:02.149 --> 00:03:03.406
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.047
Everyone should be treated fairly.

57
00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.833
Girls should be encouraged to lead.

58
00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.761
Stereotypes should be challenged.

59
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:16.395
Use 'should be' + past participle to say what is the right thing to do.

60
00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.207
Be careful! Don't say: Everyone should be treat fairly.

61
00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.816
Say: Everyone should be treated fairly.

62
00:03:26.116 --> 00:03:28.453
Use the past participle after 'be'.

63
00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.745
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:33.883
Equal Chances.

65
00:03:34.183 --> 00:03:38.353
Gender equality means everyone has the same rights and opportunity.

66
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:42.597
Education for all helps break every stereotype.

67
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.389
Girls and boys should be given the same chances.

68
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.818
Women in leadership show what is possible.

69
00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:53.483
A fair society shows respect for everyone.

70
00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:58.383
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:01.286
Everyone should be blank fairly.

72
00:04:01.586 --> 00:04:04.903
A, treated. B, treat. C, treating.

73
00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.211
The answer is A: treated.

74
00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.116
A fixed, unfair idea about a group is a blank.

75
00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:19.068
A, stereotype. B, right. C, leadership.

76
00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:25.132
The answer is A: stereotype.

77
00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:29.223
Having the same rights and chances is blank.

78
00:04:29.523 --> 00:04:33.548
A, equality. B, opportunity. C, education.

79
00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.250
The answer is A: equality.

80
00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:43.467
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.897
What can schools do to promote equality?

82
00:04:55.683 --> 00:04:57.335
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:57.635 --> 00:05:06.580
Schools can make sure everyone is treated fairly. Girls and boys should be given the same chances in sports, science and leadership.

84
00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.658
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:13.433
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and should plus passive.

86
00:05:13.733 --> 00:05:19.407
Today's value is equality. Treat everyone fairly. We all deserve the same chances.

87
00:05:19.707 --> 00:05:22.452
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

88
00:05:22.752 --> 00:05:25.787
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

